  "truth_boundary": "P is author-derived Level B measurable finite-fuel simulation infrastructure, not a standalone generic theorem printed in the source. The exact reused run retains final state, some-output or none-exhaustion, and actual query count. It inspects next even at zero fuel, and does not pad counts or turn none into a successful sample. P has natural measurable-program data, exact reply-decoder commutation, a common probability seed law and arbitrary fuel. Target measurability, run measurability, count integrability and expected-cost statements are conclusions/internal steps, not added T premises. T uses the literal fixed-spectrum full orthogonal family for d≥2 and κ≥2, the Borel Euclidean carrier and exact Option pullback sigma, with μ and program policies before O. It compares foViaMV with foRun under updateFO and mvViaFO with mvRun under updateMV separately; it does not equate runs of unrelated update policies. The genuine value/gradient reply is obtained internally from the existing producer. One public P node has this associated private T with two material P applications and no extra public-node credit. No representation of every source adaptive algorithm, guaranteed successful output, class-uniform Q_G equivalence, approximate oracle, Gaussian sampling/TV accuracy, 2T hidden-block reduction, Haar/posterior law, C6 or main lower bound is claimed. ROOT actually compiled the exact new P/T working bytes at e6bff before freezing570; this is not a retrospective build of bare e6bff or a future metadata/public tree. Independent native, blind/source implementation fidelity, reader and normal PL/V remain pending. The preproof SG/TC admission is not a new-proof source verdict. Main/shared graph/site integration, purification and Goal completion remain pending."
